  - [38;5;153mvalidate[39m with a clean form returns [38;5;153m{ valid: true, errors: {} }[39m
  - [38;5;153mvalidate[39m with several bad fields reports [1mevery[0m failing field, not just the first one
  - rule [3morder within a field[0m short-circuits — an empty password reports "required", never the [38;5;153mminLength[39m message
  - a schema field absent from [38;5;153mvalues[39m is treated as empty rather than throwing

  [1mWhat will not be tested, and I want this on the record:[0m you chose the zero-dependency option, so there's no jsdom and
  [38;5;153mbind-form.mjs[39m gets [1mno automated coverage[0m. That file is where the DOM convention, the stale-error clearing, and the
  aria attributes live — the parts most likely to break when you add form number three. I'll verify it by hand over
  [38;5;153mpython3 -m http.server[39m: submit empty (two messages appear), submit valid (login result logs, no messages), fix one
  field and resubmit (the stale message clears). I'll report exactly that and nothing stronger. Adding jsdom later is a
  one-line devDependency if you change your mind.

  [1mAlso noted:[0m you kept [38;5;153mminLength(8)[39m on the login password over my suggestion to drop it. Your call — I'll record it in
  the spec as a deliberate decision with my caveat attached, so it's visible rather than buried.

  That's the whole design. Writing it up now.

